 and children who drink water containing lead in excess of the action level could experience delays in their physical or mental development. Children could show slight deficits in attention span and learning abilities. Adults who drink this water over many years could develop kidney problems or high blood pressure.","source":"U.S. EPA, mandatory health effects language \u2014 Lead and Copper Rule","who":"Children and infants first.","kind":"contaminant","name":"Lead"}}}